# scripts/agent-gate.components — THE COMPONENT SET OF THE FULL GATE, AS DATA (issue #3544).
#
# WHY THIS FILE EXISTS. The component-set pre-flight in scripts/agent-gate.sh compares this
# branch's component set against origin/main's, so it needs main's set. It used to obtain it
# by FETCHING main's copy of agent-gate.sh and RUNNING it (`bash <fetched> --list`) — and six
# of that mechanism's seven High-severity review findings traced to that one decision, each
# fix moving the hole one layer outward (a symbolic remote name, then the validated URL, then
# the URL in argv). Per CLAUDE.md's umbrella rule (#3312): control and data must not share a
# channel when the data is attacker-controlled, and the fix is to REMOVE the channel, not to
# choose a rarer delimiter. `git show <sha>:scripts/agent-gate.components` is data by
# construction: the worst a redirected fetch can now produce is a WRONG COMPONENT LIST, which
# the comparison itself detects, rather than code execution with the developer's credentials.
#
# THE GRAMMAR IS CLOSED, and the reader REFUSES rather than guesses:
#   * one component name per line, in the gate's own dispatch order;
#   * a name matches [A-Za-z0-9._-]+ and may not start with `-`;
#   * a blank line is skipped, and a line whose FIRST character is `#` is a comment;
#   * ANYTHING else — including a name with leading or trailing whitespace — is a NAMED
#     refusal. A parser that trims is a parser that guesses.
#
# IT MUST MATCH `scripts/agent-gate.sh --list` EXACTLY, ORDER INCLUDED, and the pre-flight
# ASSERTS that on every run (`manifest-stale`, fail-closed). That local assert is what makes
# this file trustworthy as a baseline at all: without it the manifest is an unverified claim,
# and a branch that added a component here-but-not-there would leave main's manifest SHORT —
# so every later branch would compare against a too-small set and the guard would silently
# excuse real skew. Regenerate, header included:
#
#   t=$(mktemp scripts/agent-gate.components.XXXXXX) \
#     && { sed -n -e '/^[^#]/q' -e p scripts/agent-gate.components; scripts/agent-gate.sh --list; } >"$t" \
#     && mv "$t" scripts/agent-gate.components
#
# THE TEMPORARY IS CREATED BESIDE THE DESTINATION, NOT UNDER $TMPDIR (roborev job 300, Low).
# `mv` is atomic only WITHIN one filesystem. Across filesystems it degrades to copy-and-delete, and
# a reader can then observe a PARTIAL manifest — which for this file means a SHORT component set,
# i.e. exactly the silent under-count the whole guard exists to prevent. Not hypothetical on this
# fleet, measured:
#
#   ${TMPDIR:-/tmp}                 -> /dev/root
#   /data/lanes/<lane>/scripts      -> /dev/nvme1n1
#
# Two different devices, so the old form was a copy-and-delete every time. `mktemp` in `scripts/`
# keeps the O_EXCL unpredictable-name property that job 299 added AND makes the publish genuinely
# atomic. Cost: the temporary is briefly visible in a tracked directory — harmless, since it is
# `mktemp`-named, removed by the `&&` chain, and `.gitignore` need not know about it for a command
# a human runs by hand.
# THE TEMPORARY IS `mktemp`, NOT A PREDICTABLE NAME (roborev job 299, Low). This used to write
# through a fixed `/tmp/agent-gate.components`. On this fleet EVERY lane runs as the same user
# with a shared writable `/tmp`, so a same-user peer can pre-plant that path as a SYMLINK and the
# truncating `>` redirect follows it — writing the component list wherever the link points, and
# then `mv`ing an attacker-chosen file over the manifest this guard's whole verdict is derived
# from. `mktemp` creates the file itself with O_EXCL under a name it chooses, so there is nothing
# to pre-plant; the `&&` chain makes CREATION a precondition rather than an assumption (a failed
# `mktemp` must not leave the redirect writing to an empty `$t`, which is `>` on the CWD); and the
# `mv` is the atomic publish, so a reader never sees a half-written manifest. `${TMPDIR:-/tmp}`
# rather than a bare `$TMPDIR`: an unset `TMPDIR` expands to the empty string, which makes the
# path `/agent-gate.components` — the filesystem ROOT.
#
# THIS COMMAND AND THE HINT `scripts/agent-gate.sh` EMITS ON A STALE MANIFEST ARE THE SAME
# INSTRUCTION WRITTEN TWICE. Change one, change the other.
file-size
fmt
clippy
roborev-lints
core-tests
tombstones-scan
scan-offload-guard
work-counters-guard
byte-budget-guard
arrow-parity-guard
memory-budget
integration-tests
format-compat
write-tests
cli-tests
compaction-byte-parity
bti-multiclustering
query-semantics-oracle
flight-query-semantics-oracle
flight-tests
legacy-heuristics
feature-iso-parquet
feature-iso-delta-scan
python-bindings
node-bindings
binding-rust-tests
delivery-telemetry
oom-audit
parity-report
operator-metrics-doc
kit-dashboard-drift
binding-unwind-profile
